---
import DocsLayout from "../../components/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Binders — mgz-pkmn docs"
  description="The Binders tab in mgz-pkmn unifies collections (owned) and wishlists (chasing) as binder rows, with an All/Owned/Chasing filter, cover colors, and smart collections."
  current="/docs/binders"
  icon="library"
  accent="sky"
  eyebrow="Your stuff"
  heading="Binders"
  lede="The Binders tab is where the two halves of your library meet. Both your collections (owned) and your wishlists (chasing) read as binders here — one shelf for everything you keep."
>
  <h2 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">
    Owned and chasing, side by side
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-500 dark:text-sand-300">
    Rows are interleaved newest-first, each card-count visible at a glance. A kind
    badge tags every row — <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">Owned</strong>
    in palm green for collections, <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">Chasing</strong>
    in sun yellow for wishlists — and a segmented
    <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">All / Owned / Chasing</strong>
    filter scopes the list when you only want one side. Underneath they stay
    separate things; the Binders tab just gives them one home.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">
    Make it yours
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-500 dark:text-sand-300">
    Give a binder a cover color so the shelf reads at a glance, and use the
    <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">New ▾</strong>
    menu to create a collection, a wishlist, or a
    <a href="/docs/collections" class="text-palm-500 hover:text-palm-400 dark:text-sun-300 dark:hover:text-sun-200 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">smart collection</a>
    — a saved rule whose contents keep themselves current.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-palm-300 bg-palm-50 p-5 dark:border-sun-300/40 dark:bg-sun-300/5">
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-600 dark:text-sand-200">
      Not to be confused with the <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">printable 3×3 binder</strong>
      — that's an <a href="/docs/exports" class="text-palm-500 hover:text-palm-400 dark:text-sun-300 dark:hover:text-sun-200 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">export</a> you generate
      from a priced lookup to carry to a show.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
